sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant B   as Browser
    participant RLF as RateLimitingFilter
    participant LAS as LoginAttemptService
    participant SEC as Spring Security
    participant DAP as DevAuthenticationProvider
    participant DB  as PostgreSQL
    participant SES as Spring Session (Tomcat)

    Note over B,SES: BRANCH A — STAGE Profile: Local Form-Based Authentication (BCrypt)

    B   ->> RLF : POST /login {username, password}
    RLF ->> RLF : Evaluate rate limit — max 20 POST/min per source IP
    alt Rate limit exceeded
        RLF -->> B : HTTP 429 Too Many Requests
    end
    RLF ->> LAS : isLocked(username)?
    alt Account locked — 5 or more consecutive failures
        LAS -->> B : HTTP 302 /login?error (generic message — no lock state disclosed)
    end
    RLF ->> SEC : Forward to authentication filter chain
    SEC ->> DAP : authenticate(UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken)
    DAP ->> DB  : SELECT * FROM users WHERE mail = :username
    alt User record not found
        DAP ->> LAS : recordFailure(username)
        DAP -->> B  : BadCredentialsException → HTTP 302 /login?error
    end
    DAP ->> DAP : BCrypt.matches(rawPassword, storedHash)
    alt Password does not match
        DAP ->> LAS : recordFailure(username)
        DAP -->> B  : BadCredentialsException → HTTP 302 /login?error
    end
    DAP ->> LAS : recordSuccess(username)
    DAP ->> DB  : UPDATE users SET last_login_at = NOW() WHERE mail = :username
    DAP -->> SEC : UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken (principal, granted roles)
    SEC ->> SES : sessionFixation().migrateSession() — new session ID issued, prior session invalidated
    SEC ->> SES : session.setAttribute("currentUser", principal)
    SES -->> B  : HTTP 302 / — Set-Cookie: JSESSIONID=new-id; HttpOnly

    participant EB   as Browser
    participant QTA  as QTracker App
    participant AZR  as Microsoft Entra ID
    participant JWK  as Entra JWKS Endpoint
    participant DB2  as PostgreSQL
    participant SES2 as Spring Session (Tomcat)

    Note over EB,SES2: BRANCH B — Production / ssodev Profile: OAuth2 / OIDC via Entra ID (Pending: INFRA-10482)

    EB  ->> QTA  : GET /api/controls (unauthenticated)
    QTA -->> EB  : HTTP 302 → /oauth2/authorization/azure
    EB  ->> AZR  : OIDC Authorization Request (client_id, scope: openid profile email)
    Note over AZR  : Corporate user authenticates against Entra ID<br/>No password is stored in or transmitted to QTracker
    AZR -->> EB  : Authorization Code + redirect to redirect_uri
    EB  ->> QTA  : GET /login/oauth2/code/azure?code=auth_code
    QTA ->> AZR  : Token Exchange — POST /token {code, client_id, client_secret}
    AZR -->> QTA : ID Token (signed JWT) + Access Token
    QTA ->> JWK  : Validate ID Token signature via JWKS endpoint
    JWK -->> QTA : Public key confirmed — token valid and not expired
    QTA ->> DB2  : SELECT * FROM users WHERE entra_oid = :oid_claim
    Note over DB2  : users.password column NOT used in SSO mode<br/>Identity matched via entra_oid (non-secret Entra Object ID)
    DB2 -->> QTA : User record + assigned roles
    QTA ->> SES2 : Create server-side session — migrateSession()
    SES2 -->> EB : HTTP 302 / — Set-Cookie: JSESSIONID=new-id; HttpOnly; Secure
